title font5x7 -- the unifying accented-capitals font: two uppercase corpora merged, proven disjoint, GREEN
prompt Continue the autonomous loop, next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; finishing-edge: ship one whole thing before naming the next; send often.
think The prior lap closed the uppercase Latin-1 accented set (font5x7_upper_latin1, thirteen capitals) beside the acute eight (font5x7_upper_accented). The finishing-edge move is the same one the lowercase family already took: a unifying font that merges the corpora into one atlas, the capital twin of font5x7_accented and the parallel of font5x7_ascii. Ship the whole family before naming a new one.
think Mirrored font5x7_accented exactly: gather the two corpora (8 + 13), insertion-sort strictly ascending by codepoint, and prove disjointness the same honest way -- merged count equals the sum of the corpora's own count constants (acute.upper_count + rest.upper_count == 21) and the codepoints run strictly ascending with no duplicate, so a collision would fail. The band is non-contiguous (U+00C0..U+00DC skips the unaccented capitals), so the proof is ascending-and-unique rather than contiguous.
think Negative proofs guard against phantoms: a plain ASCII 'A' misses (the accented set, not the base), and an accented capital no corpus drew (U+00C5, A ring) misses too -- the font holds exactly what the two corpora drew. Every glyph carries ink; no blank in an accented set.
obs GREEN on the first metal run, no red. encoded 1005 bytes vs raw 735 (the merged accented set does not compress -- the glyphs are ink-varied, not run-dominant), reported as a fact per the REDS #82 lesson, never asserted. The lowercase and uppercase accented families now each read as one lookup: twenty-one accents, twenty-one accented capitals, every lowercase mark's capital present.
obs The two half-fonts (font5x7_accented + font5x7_upper) are the natural inputs to a later whole-Latin-1 font that also folds in the ASCII base -- named, not built this lap (finishing edge: one whole thing sent).
loom witness=font5x7_upper_witness glyphs=21 cell=5x7 encoded_bytes=1005 raw_bytes=735 round_trip=byte_identical corpora=2 sum=8+13
